      "typical_award_size": "2020 five-year plan estimated $4,353,426 from HCD, each dollar matched by the County Affordable Housing Fund; Formula Round 5 award $476,762 (March 2025); 2026-27 cycle about $477,000 PLHA plus match. HCD 2024-2028 Formula Allocation NOFA estimates: CY 2024 $509,302, CY 2025 $545,537, five-year $3,183,138. Example award: $605,062 to EAH Housing in 2024 ($302,531 PLHA plus $302,531 Trust Fund). HCD now requires 40% of new PLHA for affordable owner-occupied workforce housing (up to 150% AMI in high-cost Marin), and the County noted its owner-occupied spending was trailing.",
